       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for sertraline, which is 200 mg/day for adults. Going over that dose adds the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects. It usually doesn't add benefit. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify a higher dose.\n\nPlease check these before I enter anything:\n- **Dose:** Did you mean 40 mg, 50 mg, or 200 mg? Typical starting doses are 25\u201350 mg daily, titrated up to a maximum of 200 mg.\n- **Indication:** If the dose is intentional, what is it for? Even then, doses above 200 mg would need attending or psychiatry sign-off and documentation.\n- **Interacting drugs:** Check for other serotonergic drugs, such as SSRIs/SNRIs, tramadol, linezolid, triptans, and MAOIs. Also check for QT-prolonging drugs and anticoagulants.\n\nIf you give me a corrected dose, I'll enter it right away. If 400 mg is intended, ask your attending to confirm it. I can then enter it with a note recording that approval."
      }
